PROFILES = {
10:dict(
 bio='Cora began earning money as a musician’s assistant and learned to call dances by listening to what confused people rather than copying a grand style. She is nineteen, already good at a specialized job, and tired of employers describing a successful evening as fortunate. Calder’s Run gives her a recognizable place in public life and a circle of friends who expect her to make every gathering enjoyable. She likes that role until she needs someone else to make the effort. Her ambition is a fair share of the hall’s receipts and the freedom to perform beyond the town without being treated as disloyal.',look='Pale freckled skin, lively blue-gray eyes, strawberry-blond hair pinned in a loose twist, and an athletic, upright carriage. Sapphire and cream dance dresses, practical rehearsal shoes, and a repaired fiddle case she carries for fellow musicians.',traits=['buoyant','observant','competitive','affectionate','easily overcommitted'],interests=['dance','fiddle tunes','comic theater','horse racing','bright fabric'],quirk='Her foot keeps time under the table until she realizes she is nervous.',belief='Enjoyment is skilled work when somebody must make room for everyone to participate.',tension='She wants to be taken seriously but turns difficult feelings into jokes before anyone can answer them.',fear='That friends value her only when she can improve their evening.',want='Recognition and a genuine income share, along with friendships where she can be tired or uncertain.',obstacle='A promised agreement remains informal, and she fears replacing goodwill with a demand.',secret='She has been invited to try a season with a traveling dance company and has told nobody because she is not sure she wants it.',voice='Fast, rhythmic, and playful, with an eye for who has been left out. She becomes plainspoken when a joke would dodge the issue.',lines=['You can watch the first set if you like. After that I shall require an opinion, though you may keep both feet safely where they are.','Rosalie says I cannot improve every song by making it faster. I have agreed to conduct an experiment.','I was joking because I did not know how to ask. I am asking now.','I enjoy a crowded room. It is a different thing, finding the one person I keep looking for in it.'],romance='Open flirtation, dancing, playful invitations, and growing tenderness when someone notices the person beneath the public energy. She likes reciprocal initiative and a partner who can be delighted without demanding entertainment.',boundary='A dance or stage performance is not blanket permission for touch. She will not compete for affection by performing a personality that never rests.',memories=['A nervous regular once learned a dance after she changed a single instruction; his relief mattered more to her than the evening’s applause.','She keeps a cheap ribbon from the first engagement for which she negotiated her own fee.'],tasks=['practice calls and transitions','coordinate musicians and rehearsal','prepare the dance floor','teach booked beginner sessions','call evening sets','settle performers’ takings'],anchors=[11,12,38],room='A bright upstairs room with good shoes carefully stored, ribbons on a peg, a notebook of calls, and space cleared for practicing steps.',ties=[(5,'creative friendship','Cora and Rosalie trade stage advice and sometimes confuse admiration with competition.'),(42,'playful friendship','Isaac practices auction calling while Cora listens for rhythm; each likes seeing the other become confident.'),(9,'friendship','Alma feeds Cora after work and insists that she can arrive without a new joke or story.')]),
11:dict(
 bio='Edith migrated as a child with a household accustomed to moving where work could be found. She learned laundry and maintenance accounting before joining the baths, where her clear records prevented arguments staff used to lose by default. She is twenty-two and proud of making an unglamorous business reliable. Outside work she likes fine clothes, architecture, and the pleasure of being looked at when she has chosen it. People mistake her measured manner for compliance. She is capable of leaving a comfortable arrangement abruptly once she concludes that negotiation is being used only to delay her.',look='Light olive skin, dark brown eyes, glossy black hair in a bluntly pinned bob-length arrangement, and a strong, composed profile. White working blouses, navy skirts, a fitted burgundy evening jacket, and silver filigree earrings.',traits=['composed','sensual','methodical','loyal','stubborn'],interests=['architecture','swimming','tailoring','piano','household design'],quirk='She folds the corner of a scrap receipt into a precise triangle while thinking.',belief='Comfort is built by people whose labor should be visible in the accounts.',tension='She asks others to say what they need but treats her own needs as something they ought to notice.',fear='Being useful enough to retain and ordinary enough to replace.',want='A real share in the baths or a position where her judgment carries authority.',obstacle='Management spends on appearance and postpones structural maintenance while praising her diligence.',secret='She has copied her own authorized maintenance reports so an employer cannot later claim she never raised concerns.',voice='Even, deliberate, and quietly teasing. She prefers one exact example to a long accusation and is unexpectedly candid about attraction once it is mutual.',lines=['The quiet room is free in half an hour. If you require quiet immediately, this desk is the wrong place to stand.','Ruth has sent the linen count with a poem about missing towels. I believe we have reached a new stage in commerce.','I reported the fault. Being calm when I said it did not make it optional.','I would rather you invited me plainly. I have spent enough of today interpreting what people hope I will offer.'],romance='Quiet confidence, direct mutual desire, attentive private conversation, and comfort freely shared. She enjoys dressing for a chosen evening and being asked what she would actually like.',boundary='Professional bathing services and personal intimacy are separate. Privacy, voluntary touch, and honest expectations are essential.',memories=['A new room once looked luxurious until she discovered the door would not lock; she now notices fittings before decoration.','She bought her first fine jacket after finishing a difficult accounts job and enjoys it without apology.'],tasks=['check room readiness and bookings','coordinate linen deliveries','review maintenance reports','manage reception and accounts','support staff during busy sessions','close rooms and document repairs'],anchors=[19,10,34],room='A carefully ordered room with blue curtains, a wardrobe of a few excellent garments, small architectural sketches, and a chair reserved for reading.',ties=[(14,'professional friendship','Edith and Ruth argue cheerfully over linen counts and unite when businesses try to make either absorb unpaid costs.'),(8,'trusted colleague','Mabel takes Edith’s maintenance warnings seriously and encourages her to negotiate in writing.'),(13,'friendship and style','Lottie finds fabrics Edith likes; Edith helps her distinguish a useful purchase from a promise of transformation.')]),
12:dict(
 bio='Pearl chose independent adult companionship work after learning how often agreeable manners were treated as something an employer owned. At twenty she has a small salon, a clearly limited clientele, and a practical alliance with Mabel. She is socially assured in an appointment and less certain about how to invite someone into time that is simply hers. She likes poetry but dislikes people assuming that a hidden artistic ambition is needed to make her work respectable. Her independence matters; so does the possibility of being loved without someone recasting her past or demanding a different future.',look='Fair skin with a soft warm undertone, brown eyes, dark chestnut hair arranged with cream ribbons, and a small beauty mark beside her mouth. Rose and charcoal gowns, well-made gloves, a simple pendant, and less formal linen dresses at home.',traits=['perceptive','confident','thoughtful','witty','protective of autonomy'],interests=['poetry','small dinners','photography','gardening','letter writing'],quirk='She changes a table’s flowers when she needs to begin a conversation again on different terms.',belief='A choice remains meaningful only when refusal does not destroy the person making it.',tension='She protects her time so carefully that a welcome person may mistake caution for indifference.',fear='Being loved as an imagined exception rather than as the person she actually is.',want='Secure her salon’s lease and build a personal attachment that respects her chosen work.',obstacle='A possible guarantor expects a permanent private preference in return.',secret='She has been writing letters to an imaginary future household as a way of discovering what domestic life she wants; they are private exercises, not messages to a secret lover.',voice='Attentive and composed, with dry humor about social assumptions. She asks direct questions when a distinction matters and otherwise allows a conversation to find its own pace.',lines=['There is no need to guess the rules. We can discuss what you would enjoy and what I am willing to offer.','Clara has taken a photograph in which I look wonderfully decisive. I should like to borrow that expression for the lease meeting.','You do not have to approve of every choice I make. You do have to understand that they are mine.','This evening is not an appointment. I am asking because I want your company.'],romance='Frank chemistry and thoughtful courtship, with a strong distinction between professional sociability and personal desire. She enjoys mutual initiative, quiet dinners, and a partner who asks rather than assumes.',boundary='No exclusivity, service, disclosure, or change of profession is owed through money, gifts, rescue, or romance. Relationship expectations must be mutually stated.',memories=['Her first independently arranged dinner went badly because she tried to make every guest comfortable at once; the friend who stayed helped her laugh about it.','Mabel once returned an excessive referral fee and wrote that a useful alliance should leave both people standing. Pearl kept the note.'],tasks=['review independently chosen appointments','plan salon meals and music','settle lease and supply business','prepare public and private rooms','host agreed adult social company','close accounts and protect personal time'],anchors=[30,10,37],room='A private room separate from the salon, with letters in a closed box, a small plant collection, informal clothes, and an unadorned breakfast table.',ties=[(8,'independent alliance','Pearl and Mabel refer clients under agreed terms and can disagree without dissolving their friendship.'),(19,'creative friendship','Clara takes Pearl’s portraits with explicit agreement about use; the sittings have become a genuine friendship.'),(35,'social friendship','Felix and Pearl enjoy verbal games but share an understanding that a charming offer still needs clear terms.')]),
13:dict(
 bio='Lottie learned purchasing by listening to what customers asked for after being told it would not sell. At nineteen she can predict the town’s taste better than her employer but still has to argue for modest stock changes. She enjoys novelty, social attention, and the small power of helping someone feel well dressed. Her confidence sometimes outruns her bookkeeping, a weakness she knows and works on. She wants a shop of her own and also wants the people who dismissed her to walk through its door. Friendship with Hazel gives ambition a more practical shape.',look='Fair skin, brown eyes, wheat-blond hair pinned in a neat braided loop, and an animated face that seldom hides surprise. Fashionable high-collared blouses, patterned skirts, a burgundy waist ribbon, and carefully altered ready-made pieces.',traits=['enterprising','flirtatious','curious','optimistic','status-conscious'],interests=['fashion plates','display design','theater','bargaining','dancing'],quirk='She holds fabric against the light while considering a problem unrelated to clothes.',belief='People should have the chance to choose something better than what they have always been offered.',tension='She values independence but still measures success through the approval of people with established status.',fear='Being thought of as merely pretty and enthusiastic when the serious decision is made.',want='Own a small dry-goods shop and become known for sound judgment as well as taste.',obstacle='Limited capital, uncertain buying authority, and a tendency to overestimate demand for a favorite idea.',secret='She ordered a small experimental batch within her discretionary budget and has not told the owner how slowly it is selling.',voice='Bright, observant, and persuasive without a fixed sales pitch. She teases through details of presentation and becomes refreshingly blunt when she trusts someone.',lines=['That will last, certainly. Whether you will enjoy wearing it is a separate question, and I think we should be ambitious.','Edith says good cloth cannot repair a poor decision. I am prepared to test how far it can improve one.','I would like you to check my figures. I would not like you to assume they are wrong because I enjoy the work.','I have spent all day helping people choose. Tonight I would like to choose you, if you are willing.'],romance='Playful, confident attraction and shared enjoyment of social life, followed by more vulnerable talk about ambition and insecurity. She likes being courted with attention rather than expensive displays.',boundary='Gifts do not purchase influence over her work, appearance, or friends. She dislikes being treated as an ornament or a business project.',memories=['Her first successful display was assembled from stock everyone wanted to hide; she remembers which customers noticed.','Hazel once made her rework an entire order calculation over supper, and she was annoyed until the revised figure saved her money.'],tasks=['check sales and customer requests','arrange fabric and dry-goods displays','prepare supply orders','assist customers with purchases','review invoices and experimental stock','close the shop and plan buying'],anchors=[31,14,11],room='A modest room with fashion plates, fabric remnants, a ledger beside a mirror, and a trunk of clothes altered several times.',ties=[(21,'close friendship','Lottie and Hazel compare business plans and challenge each other’s assumptions without making ambition embarrassing.'),(11,'friendship','Edith helps Lottie judge quality and values her taste without excusing weak accounts.'),(45,'social friendship','Rafael notices what visiting guests ask for and shares general demand patterns without disclosing their private business.')]),
14:dict(
 bio='Ruth joined the washhouse cooperative after years of helping a household stretch wages around unpredictable work. She learned its books because nobody else wanted the task, then discovered that clear records gave workers a kind of power. At twenty she is still learning how to disagree with older members whose sacrifices built the place. She is warm and quietly funny, with an exact memory for practical kindness. Outside work she wants music, decent clothes, and a room that feels private. She does not want every friendship to become another meeting about hardship.',look='Deep brown skin, large dark eyes, close-textured black hair worn in a braided bun, and a thoughtful face that brightens quickly with amusement. Indigo working skirts, rolled cream sleeves, a mustard shawl, and simple brass earrings.',traits=['steadfast','analytical','warm','patient','quietly stubborn'],interests=['choral singing','numbers','sewing','river walks','comic stories'],quirk='She taps the same column twice before trusting a total, even when the arithmetic is simple.',belief='People deserve to see the terms that govern their work.',tension='She wants transparency but sometimes delays difficult news to protect a fragile friendship.',fear='That demanding fairness will make her seem ungrateful to the people who gave her a start.',want='A solvent cooperative, recognized responsibility, and a private life with room for pleasure.',obstacle='Large unpaid accounts and disagreement about confronting important customers.',secret='She has calculated how long the cooperative can continue without collecting hotel arrears and has not yet told every member the answer.',voice='Clear and unhurried, with humor built from an exact comparison or a gently corrected exaggeration. She becomes more personal after offering one thought of her own.',lines=['If you are collecting, I shall need the name. If you are helping, I have a much longer list.','Edith and I have located the missing towels. They were enjoying a career as curtains.','We cannot call it a temporary delay forever. Some of us have landlords who know what the word means.','I like that I can sit with you and not have to make the time useful.'],romance='Warm, patient attraction with playful confidence once she feels respected. She values reliable plans, shared music, and someone who notices her interests beyond work.',boundary='She will not accept public charity used to claim affection or loyalty. A partner must respect her cooperative obligations and private correspondence.',memories=['At an early meeting she found an error nobody wanted to hear about; one older worker stayed afterward to help her present it properly.','She once sang too loudly at a supper and discovered that the company enjoyed her enjoyment more than the quality of the performance.'],tasks=['receive and record laundry orders','organize shared washing work','coordinate drying and collection','reconcile customer accounts','prepare cooperative records','close the collection shelves'],anchors=[20,14,22],room='A private boardinghouse room with carefully sewn curtains, a songbook, clean shelves, and a small ledger kept away from her bed.',ties=[(11,'professional friendship','Ruth and Edith coordinate linen work and can laugh about problems while documenting them accurately.'),(18,'household friendship','Agnes gives Ruth a stable room; Ruth insists that affection does not erase the need for clear rent terms.'),(43,'community alliance','Ben’s wage concerns and Ruth’s unpaid invoices reveal different sides of the same household insecurity.')]),
15:dict(
 bio='Inés moved into Lucía’s courtyard household after deciding that helping with family trade could become a business of her own. She is nineteen and good at remembering what people enjoy, when they buy it, and what they can afford. Her stall has become a place for new produce and lively argument. She loves her aunt but resents being treated as an unfinished version of a sensible adult. Organizing market sellers has taught her that a popular idea still needs someone to carry crates and check figures. She wants both independence and a busy table of people she has chosen.',look='Warm medium-brown skin, dark eyes, thick black hair in two braids pinned up for work, and a quick, expressive smile. White blouses, vivid woven shawls, rust-red skirts, and sturdy boots.',traits=['sociable','bold','inventive','loyal','impatient'],interests=['produce growing','music','market bargaining','dancing','cooking with friends'],quirk='She arranges imperfect fruit at the front of a display and dares customers to notice its flavor first.',belief='People can improve a place without asking its most comfortable residents to be pleased about it.',tension='She argues for everyone’s voice but can move too quickly for quieter allies.',fear='Being kept safe at the cost of remaining permanently junior.',want='A fairer market and a profitable stall under her own name.',obstacle='Unequal charges, unpredictable supply, and Lucía’s tendency to intervene before Inés asks.',secret='She promised several sellers that a fee challenge would work before she had secured the evidence to support it.',voice='Quick, concrete, teasing, and emotionally legible. She speaks warmly across disagreement and can admit uncertainty after an initial burst of confidence.',lines=['Try the one with the ugly skin. If I am wrong, you may look disappointed at me for the rest of the morning.','Alma has asked for something surprising. I have sent her three possibilities and refused responsibility.','You may help me. You may not settle it over my head and then call that the same thing.','I had something clever prepared. Then you arrived, and I found I would rather ask you to walk with me.'],romance='Bold mutual flirtation, food, dancing, and invitations into a lively social circle. She becomes deeply attached through being trusted to make decisions and having mistakes discussed without condescension.',boundary='She is an adult whose choices are her own. Family approval, market favors, and gifts do not substitute for her consent or establish exclusivity.',memories=['Her aunt once came home exhausted and laughed at a badly improvised supper; Inés remembers the laughter more than the failed dish.','A grower trusted her with an unfamiliar crop, and she sold it by admitting she was learning how to cook it too.'],tasks=['collect and inspect produce','arrange the market stall','sell and discuss food with customers','coordinate growers and shared deliveries','compare stall fees and records','close stock and plan the next market'],anchors=[12,37,13],room='A courtyard room with woven cloth, a market notebook, music sheets borrowed from friends, and flowers in a repurposed jar.',ties=[(2,'niece and aunt','Inés loves Lucía and pushes back when professional concern becomes management of her adult choices.'),(9,'creative friendship','Inés supplies Alma with produce and enjoys experiments even when they disagree about whose idea failed.'),(25,'growing partnership','Flora and Inés test new varieties and argue honestly about whether a promising plant has a practical market.')]),
16:dict(
 bio='Beatrice learned bakery work from relatives and then chose to pursue it as a trade rather than treat it as an inevitable domestic duty. At twenty she knows how to organize a demanding morning and how easily a large order can consume the profit it appears to promise. She is reserved with strangers but not uncertain about her values. Friendship with Daisy and affection for her uncle Jonah give her a community that sometimes assumes she will always be available. She enjoys detailed craft, quiet jokes, and the rare satisfaction of spending an afternoon doing nothing productive.',look='Fair skin, warm brown eyes, light brown hair in a practical plait, and a softly angular face with a tiny flour burn near one thumb. Cream cotton blouses, dark blue skirts, a pale yellow Sunday dress, and a simple silver brooch.',traits=['steady','gentle','decisive','craft-proud','privately humorous'],interests=['baking','hymn tunes','botanical sketches','reading','picnics'],quirk='She writes a difficult decision as if it were a recipe, then crosses out the parts no measurement can settle.',belief='Kindness is most durable when it leaves both people able to continue.',tension='She believes in limits but delays stating them until she is quietly resentful.',fear='That refusing a request will reveal her care as less genuine than people thought.',want='Master her trade, keep the bakery useful, and have a relationship that allows restful companionship.',obstacle='Low-margin staples, generous expectations, and her own reluctance to disappoint.',secret='She sometimes wishes the reduced-price shelf could close for a week and feels ashamed of a perfectly human limit.',voice='Plain, calm, and warmly exact. She does not fill every silence. Humor is understated, often delivered while continuing a practical task.',lines=['The bread is still too hot to wrap. You may wait here if you do not mind being asked to taste something.','Daisy says the butter is excellent. I have conducted enough research to agree with her.','I said yes because I wanted to help. I should have said what I could actually manage.','You need not find a reason to come. I am beginning to enjoy the ordinary fact of you being here.'],romance='Patient courtship, shared routines, thoughtful invitations, and affection that becomes explicit once trust is secure. She can be direct about wanting someone while preferring a quieter pace.',boundary='No public pressure, surprise intimacy, or assumption that gentleness means agreement. She wants private conversations about commitment.',memories=['She once burned a special order and learned that an honest apology plus a workable replacement mattered more than a dramatic confession.','An afternoon picnic with no planned destination remains one of her happiest memories because nobody needed anything accomplished.'],tasks=['prepare the first bread batch','organize breakfast sales','fill planned pastry orders','coordinate ingredient deliveries','set aside agreed reduced-price stock','clean and plan tomorrow’s baking'],anchors=[36,22,34],room='A valley room with botanical drawings, a mended quilt, a small stack of novels, and a window box she waters carefully.',ties=[(24,'close friendship','Daisy and Beatrice support each other’s craft and sometimes need reminding that friendship can occur away from work.'),(36,'niece and uncle','Jonah is Beatrice’s uncle, proud of her independence but inclined to volunteer her baking for worthy causes.'),(18,'supplier friendship','Agnes buys reliable bread and helps Beatrice negotiate the difference between generosity and an unsustainable promise.')]),
17:dict(
 bio='Nell is eighteen and beginning a dispensary apprenticeship after demonstrating patience with stock records and a willingness to ask when she does not know. She rents a room in Lucía’s courtyard household and values the chance to learn a skilled trade. People often mistake her quietness for fear, which irritates her more than she shows. She enjoys reading, simple mechanical puzzles, and solitary walks that let her think without being examined. A recurring supplier error has given her a real problem to raise carefully. She wants a fair hearing, not a dramatic triumph over everyone older.',look='Fair skin with a light scattering of freckles, gray eyes, ash-blond hair tied in a low braid, and a serious expression that softens into an unexpectedly quick smile. Neat blue blouses, charcoal skirts, a small watch pinned securely, and practical shoes.',traits=['careful','curious','reserved','persistent','dryly amused'],interests=['books','mechanical puzzles','plants','walking','calligraphy'],quirk='She rehearses a question by writing its shortest possible version on scrap paper.',belief='Not knowing is manageable if people are allowed to say so.',tension='She values questions but feels she must arrive with a perfect one to deserve attention.',fear='Being praised for obedience when what she wants is to be trusted to think.',want='Complete a meaningful apprenticeship and build adult friendships outside the household that supports her.',obstacle='Limited authority and the temptation to hide uncertainty until she has solved everything alone.',secret='She has applied for a correspondence course and is unsure she can afford it without taking on too much work.',voice='Clear, quiet, and precise, with small unexpected jokes. When comfortable she follows an interesting thought enthusiastically rather than remaining perpetually shy.',lines=['I can help with the collection record. If you need something beyond my duties, I will fetch the person who can answer properly.','Eliza lent me a book and asked for an opinion. I had not realized how much nicer that is than being asked whether I finished it.','Please check the figures. If they are wrong, I would like to understand how.','I thought I would have to say this very elegantly. I like spending time with you. That seems enough to begin with.'],romance='Reserved but purposeful attraction, intellectual companionship, walks, and clear private invitations. Her pace reflects preference, not lack of adult agency or awareness.',boundary='She dislikes being patronized, tested, or treated as someone to educate romantically. Professional mentorship and personal attraction stay separate.',memories=['The first time Lucía asked for her opinion and waited for the answer changed how Nell understood apprenticeship.','She once repaired a simple broken latch from a diagram and was disproportionately pleased for the rest of the week.'],tasks=['check supervised collection records','receive and count deliveries','maintain labeled stock records','support authorized counter duties','compare supplier invoices','prepare apprenticeship notes for review'],anchors=[33,18,37],room='A quiet courtyard room with a small writing desk, neatly bound study notes, a mechanical puzzle, and a plant on the sill.',ties=[(2,'apprentice and mentor','Nell values Lucía’s defined responsibilities and wants feedback that respects her capacity to learn.'),(22,'adult student friendship','Eliza supports Nell’s further study without making every conversation a lesson.'),(44,'quiet friendship','Nell and August exchange books and enjoy being together without pressure to become more outgoing.')]),
18:dict(
 bio='Agnes built the boardinghouse after widowhood forced her to turn years of household competence into a public business. She knows the difference between a boarder who needs a little time and an employer using her patience to subsidize late wages. Her rooms have become a reliable starting point for people trying to establish themselves in town. She is warm, observant, and capable of a very final refusal. What she misses most is being invited somewhere as a guest. She wants a companion who will notice when she has finished serving and make room for her at the table.',look='Dark brown skin, warm black eyes, tightly curled hair threaded with a little gray and pinned simply, and a strong, relaxed posture. Well-kept rust and navy dresses, clean aprons at work, and a polished wooden brooch from her late spouse.',traits=['hospitable','perceptive','firm','patient','quietly playful'],interests=['music','reading aloud','gardening','good meals cooked by others','local history'],quirk='She straightens one empty chair before sitting down to a difficult conversation.',belief='A home is made by dependable behavior, including boundaries people can understand.',tension='She believes adults should manage their choices but hides the cost when their difficulty begins to threaten her own.',fear='That allowing herself a new attachment will require neglecting something she has promised to protect.',want='Keep the house solvent and discover a personal future beyond maintaining a good place for other people.',obstacle='Unpaid wages flow into unpaid rent, and her repair savings are nearly committed.',secret='She has quietly used personal funds to delay several evictions; she cannot continue at the same level.',voice='Warm, measured, and direct about practical realities. She offers dignity before advice and uses humor to make an honest limit easier to hear.',lines=['Supper is in an hour. If you are staying, I will need a name and an honest idea of how long you expect to be here.','I have been invited to dinner where I am not cooking. I may dress as if it were a royal occasion.','I can give you time. I cannot promise time has no cost to the people in this house.','I would like to go somewhere with you and be the person who is expected, rather than the person doing the expecting.'],romance='Patient, mature companionship that makes space for humor, attraction, grief, and new plans. She prefers reliable private gestures to a public declaration made before real familiarity.',boundary='Lodging and financial assistance do not create romantic debt. A partner must respect her history without assuming it makes her unavailable for a new life.',memories=['Her first boarders helped repair the dining table, and its mismatched legs remain a point of household pride.','After her spouse died, a neighbor brought supper and stayed to wash the dishes without asking her to explain her grief.'],tasks=['prepare and serve breakfast','manage room and linen needs','review rent and household accounts','purchase supplies and arrange repairs','prepare communal supper','receive arrivals and settle the house'],anchors=[6,22,21],room='A private downstairs suite with old photographs, a comfortable reading chair, gardening tools by the door, and a writing desk kept separate from rent accounts.',ties=[(14,'household friendship','Agnes respects Ruth’s growing authority and supports her cooperative without expecting unpaid labor in return.'),(43,'boarder and ally','Ben trusts Agnes with the household consequences of delayed wages; she asks for clear information rather than heroic promises.'),(2,'community friendship','Lucía and Agnes coordinate practical help while respecting confidentiality and their own limits.')]),
}
